# Don't ignore anything - we need all files.
#
# One exception. .env.local is gitignored but was still being uploaded on a
# CLI deploy, because this file excluded nothing. The build reads its own
# environment from the Vercel project settings, so the local copy has no
# business being there: if the two ever drift, the build silently picks up
# whatever REACT_APP_ADMIN_SECRET happens to be on the machine that deployed.
#
# Vercel's own env vars still win over a .env file at build time, so this was
# not breaking anything today. It removes the way it could.
.env.local
.env.*.local
